  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Agriculture obligated $8.7B in contracts in FY2026 to date. Current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). Obligations are down 9.0% year over year while the agency executed 26,217 awards at an average award size of $332K. Spending has trended from $9.7B in FY21 up to $11.6B in FY24, then down to $9.6B in FY25 and to $8.7B in FY26. The largest buying categories in FY2026 to date include Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation at $960M, Support Activities for Forestry at $628M, and Animal (except Poultry) Slaughtering at $522M. The top vendors reflect those category patterns, led by KIEWIT INFRASTRUCTURE SOUTH CO at $261M, PERIMETER SOLUTIONS LP at $227M, and TYSON FOODS INC. at $208M. The mix shows a significant share for transportation, forestry support, food processing, and selected IT services such as Computer Systems Design Services at $422M and Other Computer Related Services at $386M. This snapshot reflects a partial fiscal year and a reduced obligations level compared with the prior fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have obligations changed year over year?",
        "body": "The Department of Agriculture obligated $8.7B in FY2026 to date. Obligations are down 9.0% year over year. Obligations rose from $9.7B in FY21 to $11.6B in FY24 before falling to $9.6B in FY25 and $8.7B in FY26. The current total is a partial fiscal year figure."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are Agriculture's biggest buying categories now?",
        "body": "Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation is the largest category at $960M in FY2026 to date. Support Activities for Forestry is $628M and Animal (except Poultry) Slaughtering is $522M. The agency also shows major spending in Computer Systems Design Services at $422M and Fruit and Vegetable Canning at $498M."
      }
    ]
